<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Capetian House of Anjou</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Angevins of Naples, Angevin dynasty of Naples</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Capetian House of Anjou was a branch of the French royal family founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-i-of-anjou">Charles of Anjou</a>, brother of Louis IX. Charles conquered the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> in 1266 but lost the island in the Sicilian Vespers of 1282, after which his descendants ruled the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> until 1435. Another line, beginning with Charles Robert in 1308, ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> and, under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-i-of-hungary">Louis the Great</a>, also <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/capetian-house-of-anjou.jpg" alt="Capetian House of Anjou" width="320" height="374" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carlodangio · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arms_of_Jean_dAnjou.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
